@startuml http_session_execution_controls
title HTTP Session Execution Control Design

' Source evidence (pi-mono commit 086c32e74530564922d011ade23ff582c9d63116):
' packages/coding-agent/src/core/agent-session.ts, steer, followUp, clearQueue, and abort,
' lines 1336-1404 and 1516-1556
' packages/agent/src/agent.ts, steer, followUp, abort, and queue drain order,
' lines 275-319, 350-390, and 456-492
' packages/coding-agent/src/modes/rpc/rpc-mode.ts, steer, follow_up, and abort,
' lines 418-430
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java commit 8691e8800f05f28afe22499050c29220ef5b7475):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/session/RuntimeSessionControlService.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSessionControlController.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeActiveExecution.java.
' Observed behavior: pi keeps separate steering and follow-up queues, drains steering first,
' and aborts the current in-process run. Java now exposes text-only steer, follow-up, and abort.
' Observed behavior: three HTTP operations use Session scope because no public Run exists.
' Product constraint: v1 accepts text only, fixes one-at-a-time FIFO behavior, and projects
' a delivered control message as the existing durable user.message entry type.
' Product constraint: all Runtime operations carry integration-context headers without local validation.
' Design reason: separate control responses from the existing POST Events SSE response.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  ActorBorderColor #475569
  ActorFontColor #0F172A
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
  GroupBorderColor #64748B
  GroupFontColor #334155
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7ED
  BorderColor #C2410C
  FontColor #7C2D12
}

actor Caller
participant "Session Control\nAPI" as API
database "Runtime Session\nStore" as Store
collections "Active Execution\nQueues" as Queue
participant "AgentSession" as Session
participant "Existing POST Events\nSSE Stream" as SSE
participant ResultBeanAdapter

group Queue a Steering Message
  Caller -> API : POST /sessions/{session_id}/steers\ncontext headers and message only
  API -> API : do not validate integration credentials
  API -> Store : require running Session
  Store --> API : active execution handle
  API -> Queue : append Steer atomically in FIFO order
  Queue --> API : accepted_at
  API -> ResultBeanAdapter : normal(ControlAcceptedResponseVO)
  ResultBeanAdapter --> API : resCode, resMsg, result
  API --> Caller : 202 Accepted
end

group Queue a FollowUp Message
  Caller -> API : POST /sessions/{session_id}/follow-ups\ncontext headers and message only
  API -> API : do not validate integration credentials
  API -> Store : require running Session
  Store --> API : active execution handle
  API -> Queue : append FollowUp atomically in FIFO order
  Queue --> API : accepted_at
  API -> ResultBeanAdapter : normal(ControlAcceptedResponseVO)
  ResultBeanAdapter --> API : resCode, resMsg, result
  API --> Caller : 202 Accepted
end

alt current Assistant turn and tools complete with Steer queued
  Session -> Queue : drain one Steer before FollowUp
  Queue --> Session : next user message
  Session -> Store : append durable user.message on delivery
  Store --> SSE : user.message with entry_id and entry_seq
  Session -> Session : continue with next model invocation
else Agent would stop and only FollowUp is queued
  Session -> Queue : drain one FollowUp
  Queue --> Session : next user message
  Session -> Store : append durable user.message on delivery
  Store --> SSE : user.message with entry_id and entry_seq
  Session -> Session : continue active execution
end

group Abort current execution idempotently
  Caller -> API : POST /sessions/{session_id}/abort\ncontext headers and no request body
  API -> API : do not validate integration credentials
  API -> Store : load Session
  Store --> API : active execution or idle
  opt execution is active
    API -> Session : abort model, tools, and subagents
    API -> Queue : clear undelivered Steer and FollowUp
    API -> Session : wait for idle
    Session --> SSE : session.status.idle
    Session --> SSE : stream.end reason aborted
  end
  API --> Caller : 204 No Content after idle
end

note over API,Queue
Steer and FollowUp require a running Session.
An idle request returns 409 SESSION_NOT_RUNNING.
Abort on an idle Session is a successful no-op.
No control id or public Run resource is created.
end note
@enduml

@startuml http_execution_resource_model
title Session Event, Internal Execution, and Entry Recovery Boundary

' Source evidence verified on 2026-08-17:
' https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/events-and-streaming
' https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/sessions
' pi-mono packages/coding-agent/src/core/session-manager.ts, getBranch and appendMessage
' pi-mono-java commit 8691e8800f05f28afe22499050c29220ef5b7475,
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventService.java
' Observed behavior: both pi baselines rebuild conversation context from messages and entries.
' Observed behavior: CampusClaw exposes Session Events and keeps execution identity internal.
' Design reason: one public recovery model avoids duplicated lifecycle and cursor semantics.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 16
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam defaultFontColor #0F172A
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #64748B
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  FontColor #0F172A
}

actor Caller
rectangle "POST /sessions/{id}/events\nmessage and file_ids, direct SSE" as SendEvent
rectangle "ActiveExecution\ninternal Session state" as Execution
rectangle "Transient Preview\nstarted, delta, tool lifecycle" as Preview
rectangle "Persisted Entry\nentry_id and entry_seq" as Entry
rectangle "GET /sessions/{id}/events\ncurrent-branch recovery" as GetEvents
rectangle "Session Controls\nsteer, follow-up, abort" as Controls

Caller --> SendEvent : submit one user input
SendEvent --> Execution : accept and start
Execution --> Preview : stream live progress
Execution --> Entry : commit authoritative facts
Entry --> GetEvents : recover after disconnect
Caller --> Controls : independent HTTP requests
Controls --> Execution : queue or cancel

note bottom of Execution
Execution has no caller-visible identity.
Session state is idle or running.
end note

note bottom of GetEvents
user.message, assistant.message.completed, and tool.result are eligible.
assistant.thinking.completed depends on current Session thinking.
end note
@enduml
